    {
      "id": "claim_474008372aed4c8480ee808c41a8bf0d",
      "statement": "The SQLite path is constructed from the process working directory captured at module import plus the literal `\\\\test.db`; because that backslash is platform-dependent, the database location can vary with both launch directory and operating system. The startup health check creates `Profiles` only when the table is absent, does not validate or migrate an existing schema, and returns no truthy success value, so `entry.py`'s `if not dbHealthCheck()` warning condition is always taken.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://noFrontEnd/dbFuns.py#L5-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a559caea5f838d21997d446d456de87aca125cc9a74bb1043c2cf5b30cf2020f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://noFrontEnd/entry.py#L9-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9baabcbc9b3a8eccdf2dfaa188864654a64598812e53883baf64d1c598707c80:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_46c00d75b68c4d53a6ee7274ae4e8a3c",
      "statement": "The profile schema declares `USERNAME` as the primary key and stores `AGE` and `EMAIL`; `dbNewUserfun` also creates a username-derived `<username>_stats` table with a date, four left/right exercise-count fields, and eight side-specific maximum/minimum angle fields. The stats table has no declared primary key, date uniqueness constraint, or foreign key to `Profiles`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://noFrontEnd/dbFuns.py#L14-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1ef3a0525be02bd8bb4b41c87b95a7f080589ed0cd78c2c36ba27864f8e2a63c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://noFrontEnd/dbFuns.py#L52-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e36f9586d2e7182e848680514f8916d7b2dd0f7d5a03644d5b6c7993e5091da:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b322fca3fe324fa898650b80cdf1a51b",
      "statement": "`dbUpdatefun` implements additive per-day aggregation: it selects today's row in the user's stats table, inserts a date plus twelve zero values when none is found, increments the caller-selected field, and commits the operation on a per-call connection. Because count updates for left and right sides are separate calls, they are not atomic as one workout; without date uniqueness, concurrent select-then-insert calls can also create duplicate daily rows, and an update affects all matching-date rows.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://noFrontEnd/dbFuns.py#L33-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c290873546193fa4f94860c2420c86936fc70919ab4ca2879973fe0fef42581b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://noFrontEnd/front.py#L57-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3436fc57ab8caacb590740630e15d8ff2b3f961e374bfd86e24b1103ed7e056c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
