    {
      "id": "claim_23d05dbd7546495881be75d7df250844",
      "statement": "Profile creation inserts the profile and creates its per-user table using one connection and commits after both statements, while signup duplicate checks happen earlier through separate reads; there is no explicit exception handling or guaranteed connection cleanup around those operations, and a check-then-insert race can still meet the username primary-key constraint.",
